+"you confirm as actual bleeding enter future calculations. Click a drop for "
+"today or an earlier day and explicitly select the bleeding intensity "
+"actually observed. Confirmation records only that day and recalculates the "
+"estimate. Future days cannot be confirmed; Cancel leaves your records "
+"unchanged.</p><p>When hints are enabled, a separate pale dashed drop may "
+"appear at the earlier estimated start after the forecast expires. Its "
+"tooltip only says that no new start is recorded; it does not prove a missed "
+"period. Dashed drops can also explain changes or uncertainty in recorded "
+"intervals and bleeding. They never count as entries.</p><h3>Details and "
+"limitations</h3><p>Calculated from at least three starts. Bleeding entries "
+"up to three days apart form one episode. After an interval outside 14–60 "
+"days, two new intervals are needed. The window spans the shortest and "
+"longest of up to twelve recent intervals, plus two days on either side.</"
+"p><p>Estimate from your entries, not a diagnosis or contraception method. "
+"Seek medical advice for new, persistent or distressing changes.</p><h3>Pause "
+"forecasts</h3><p>Click a dashed drop and choose pregnancy, breastfeeding, "
+"medication/hormonal treatment, perimenopause/menopause, or another reason. "
+"Pregnancy initially suggests nine calendar months from recording the pause; "
+"this is not a due date. Other reasons initially have no fixed end. For every "
+"reason you can change the end date or leave it open.</p><p>The pause "
+"includes its final day; without a date it remains until explicitly ended. "
+"Forecasts, missing-start hints and cycle reminders stop, while a neutral "
+"status shows the reason and end. New observed bleeding is saved, but the "
+"pause ends only if you separately confirm it as a new period. Keep pause or "
+"cancelling that question preserves both the bleeding record and the pause. "
+"Ending the pause manually resumes planning today without creating a bleeding "
+"entry.</p><p>After resumption, only entries from the resumption day, or "
+"after the scheduled end, form the new history. Three new starts are needed; "
+"old cycles do not produce an overdue warning. Confirm bleeding as a new "
+"period only if that is how it has been identified. Bleeding during pregnancy "
+"needs prompt medical advice; bleeding after menopause also needs medical "
+"assessment. Ending a planning pause does not establish that a pregnancy or "
+"menopause has ended.</p>"
